   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h3> »sawCheck« </h3> <h1> Precision in Saw Blade Measurement </h1>",
   "body": "<p><strong>The manufacture and regrinding of precision saw blades are subject to ever-increasing requirements for accuracy and cost-effectiveness. </strong></p> <p>With the »sawCheck« inspection and measuring machine, ZOLLER offers a solution for measuring saw blades fully automatically, tooth by tooth, with high precision, and user-independent. During tooth inspection, parameters such as tooth profile, pitch, radial run-out, and cutting height can be measured using transmitted light. Using incident light, parameters such as rake angle, radial relief angle, tooth thickness, center offset, or wear and tear—whether radial or axial—can be quickly inspected and documented in detail, all user-independent and quickly.</p> <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/ca/company/contact\">Inquire Now</a></p>",
